# DinoBoard Eval Model

Use `scripts/eval_model.py` for model strength checks, heuristic baselines,
random-init sanity tests, and replay generation.

## Defaults

- `--model` is the measured side in the printed W-L-D summary.
- Bare `heuristic` resolves through `heuristic.json::selectors[--heuristic-selector]`.
- The measured side rotates by `game_idx % num_players` unless `--fixed-seat`
  or `--paired-seats` is used.
- Model-involved eval defaults to the same batched evaluator config as training
  self-play when `train.json::training.selfplay_concurrency.enabled=true`.
- Pass `--providers coreml,cpu` on Apple or `--providers cuda,cpu` on NVIDIA
  to override the JSON provider list for a run.
- Use `--no-save` for benchmark sweeps unless replay JSON is needed.

## Common Commands

Model vs heuristic:

```bash
python3 scripts/eval_model.py --game carcassonne \
  --model games/carcassonne/model/carcassonne_2p.onnx \
  --opponent heuristic --games 100 --workers 100 \
  --sims 1000 --profile eval --providers coreml,cpu \
  --no-save -o /tmp/eval
```

Heuristic as measured side:

```bash
python3 scripts/eval_model.py --game carcassonne \
  --model heuristic \
  --opponent games/carcassonne/model/carcassonne_2p.onnx \
  --name-model rule_mcts --name-opponent model \
  --games 100 --workers 100 --sims 1000 --profile eval \
  --providers coreml,cpu --no-save -o /tmp/eval
```

Model vs model:

```bash
python3 scripts/eval_model.py --game coup \
  --model runs/coup/models/model_latest.onnx --name-model latest \
  --opponent runs/coup/models/model_best.onnx --name-opponent best \
  --games 40 --workers 40 --providers cuda,cpu \
  --no-save -o /tmp/eval
```

## Pitfalls

- `--sims` controls ONNX model-seat MCTS only. Heuristic MCTS-PV sims come
  from `heuristic.json`; temporary heuristic sim changes must be restored.
- Batched eval accelerates ONNX leaf inference only. Tree search and
  hand-written heuristic PV evaluation remain CPU work.
- Confirm the launch prints `Using batched eval` before trusting a long GPU
  benchmark.
- `--no-batched` is a legacy/debug path and can multiply ONNX memory by worker
  count.
